  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering ASEANs Efforts to Prevent and Combat Trafficking in Persons in Southeast Asia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will support ASEAN&apos;s efforts to prevent and combat trafficking in persons by strengthening ASEAN&apos;s capacity. The program has three objectives: 1.) strengthening ASEAN&apos;s capacity to address TIP in the region through the harmonization of laws among member states by encouraging Burma, Brunei, Malaysia, Singapore, and Vietnam to accede to the Palermo protocols and adoption of TIP language to match the Palermo protocol; 2.) build awareness, understanding, and capacity among government and law enforcement within ASEAN on TIP; and 3.) strengthen regional sharing of information and collaboration with an emphasis on standards of care for TIP victims.</narrative>
  </description>
